# Test-driven development

Use this skill to select and prove a regression test when a consumer-visible contract can be tested. For an unexpected failure, first use `systematic-debugging` to establish the cause. Then state the expected behavior and boundary; add or identify a deterministic test that would catch the missing behavior. Confirm a new regression test fails for the expected reason before fixing it, but do not rerun a failure the user has already reported as ground truth.

Implement the smallest change that passes. Run the focused test, then the broader relevant suite when appropriate; refactor only while tests remain green. If a useful failing-first test is impractical, use a direct scenario instead. `verification-before-completion` owns the final smoke check and evidence report; do not add tautological tests for forwarding, copies, or incidental defaults.
